---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Image Identifier handles your images, local analysis, and network requests for assets and optional models."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-fg m-0">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Image Identifier is built to analyze the image you select in your browser. Your selected image
      bytes are not uploaded to an application backend for analysis, and we do not send them to a
      third-party detector API as part of the core tool.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">What stays local</h2>
    <ul class="text-muted pl-5 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>The file you choose is read in the browser for validation and review.</li>
      <li>Results you see come from checks running on your device for that session.</li>
      <li>We do not create accounts or store your images in a cloud gallery.</li>
      <li>We do not save image contents, prompts, or location fields to localStorage by default.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">What may use the network</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      “Analyzes locally” is not the same as “never uses the network.” The site may still request:
    </p>
    <ul class="text-muted pl-5 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>Static site assets (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, fonts, icons).</li>
      <li>Runtime modules required by the tool (including WebAssembly binaries hosted with the app).</li>
      <li>
        An optional model download if you explicitly start the statistical check (first run or after
        cache eviction).
      </li>
      <li>Analytics or advertising scripts only if they are enabled later — none are required for the tool to work today.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Those requests should not include your selected image bytes. Before a public release with ads or
      analytics, the Network panel should be re-checked while running all analysis paths.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Sensitive fields</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      If a file may contain location-related fields, they stay hidden until you choose to reveal them
      in the results view.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-fg mt-10 mb-3">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-muted leading-relaxed">
      Privacy questions: see the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-muted">
      <a href="/">← Back to the tool</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
